fix(startup): park the hidden Steam webview off-screen

Every launch flashed a translucent rectangle over the main window.
The cause was the hidden Steam WebView2 host: `visible(false)` is not
enough for a WebView2 window, because the control keeps its own
composition surface and DWM keeps compositing it even while the
window's WS_VISIBLE bit is clear.

Measured with an A/B capture: with the window merely hidden the artefact
covers the whole main window; moving that same window to x=-32000 makes
it disappear entirely (34,959 differing pixels, spanning the 1250x900
window area at 125% DPI).

So create it parked off-screen as well as hidden. Every visible path
(`show_login`, `reveal`, `goto_login_form`, `login_fill`) now re-centres
it first, otherwise the login window would open off-screen and the
button would look dead.

This also explains why `IsWindowVisible` reported false throughout the
investigation: the window really was hidden, it was just still being
composited.

Gates: cargo test 52, clippy 0 warnings, tsc 0, eslint 0, vitest 113.